==German==

===Etymology===
{{dercat|de|gem-pro|ine-pro|inh=1}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|spīen}}, from {{inh|de|goh|spīwan}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*spīwan}}. Compare {{cog|nl|spuwen}}, {{m|nl|spugen}}, {{cog|en|spew}}, {{cog|da|spy}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʃpaɪ̯ən/}}
* {{audio|de|De-speien.ogg|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|speien<spie,gespien>}}

# to [[spit]]
#: {{syn|de|spucken}}
# {{lb|de|euphemistic}} to [[vomit]]
#: {{syn|de|kotzen}}

====Conjugation====
{{de-conj|speien<spie,gespien>}}
* The past participle currently has two different pronunciations: one corresponding to {{m|de|gespien}} {{IPAchar|[ɡəˈʃpiːn]}} and the other to {{m|de|gespieen}} {{IPAchar|[ɡəˈʃpiːən]}}. Today, though, the only official spelling is {{m|de||gespien}}, regardless of pronunciation.
* Similary the conjunctive (subjunctive) is spelled {{m|de|spiee}} or {{m|de|spie}}. Both are pronounced {{IPAchar|[ˈʃpiːə]}}, but only the latter spelling is official nowadays.

